WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.215
Same cheese.

00:00:01.215 --> 00:00:02.229
Same case.

00:00:02.229 --> 00:00:04.900
Forty eight dollars became fifty six.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.624
You've got a restaurant to run.

00:00:08.624 --> 00:00:12.550
Start with one check, using
the paperwork you already have.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.953
Here's a sample invoice.

00:00:15.953 --> 00:00:19.283
The vendor, date,
number and total are there.

00:00:19.283 --> 00:00:23.400
The pack is unclear, so it
asks: pounds or kilograms?

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.175
That's eight dollars more per case.

00:00:28.175 --> 00:00:29.844
Eighty more for ten cases.

00:00:29.844 --> 00:00:33.350
Open the original lines and check
the change with your rep.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.766
Labor works from the schedule
and clock report.

00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:43.850
Extra hours and fewer hours stay separate,
so you can ask what happened.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.984
Check one menu item, too.

00:00:48.984 --> 00:00:53.716
This sample pizza uses four dollars in
ingredients at a sixteen dollar menu price.

00:00:53.716 --> 00:00:55.500
Labor and overhead are separate.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.281
Your first owner seat is free.

00:00:59.281 --> 00:01:01.684
No card or inbox connection to start.

00:01:01.684 --> 00:01:03.119
Get one useful answer.

00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:05.200
Open your workspace when you're ready.
